WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:11.052
In tutorial 9.6, you'll answer
replies, and record the links you win.

00:00:12.185 --> 00:00:15.240
First, on Link building,
click In progress.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:19.828
Each conversation shows how many e-mails
have gone out, and what happens next.

00:00:20.822 --> 00:00:23.347
Click Show the thread
to read what you sent.

00:00:23.397 --> 00:00:27.911
Pause holds a conversation, Resume
picks it up again, and Stop ends it.

00:00:28.906 --> 00:00:33.356
To change a follow-up before it
goes, click Edit the unsent e-mails.

00:00:33.406 --> 00:00:35.697
E-mails already sent stay as they were.

00:00:36.721 --> 00:00:40.381
Next, open Replies. Each
reply is sorted for you,

00:00:40.431 --> 00:00:42.533
with a short summary of what they said.

00:00:43.692 --> 00:00:46.542
Here, they're interested.
Read their reply,

00:00:46.592 --> 00:00:49.224
then edit the suggested
answer in your own words.

00:00:51.171 --> 00:00:54.796
Then click Send in this thread.
It goes from your own mailbox,

00:00:54.846 --> 00:00:57.276
signed with your name, title and company.

00:00:58.692 --> 00:01:02.517
Some replies need care. A
request for payment is flagged,

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:05.227
and a no puts the address
on your opt-out list.

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:10.817
When they add your link, click Mark
won, or Not a fit if it isn't for you.

00:01:10.867 --> 00:01:14.066
The link is checked on their
page, then it counts as won.

00:01:15.117 --> 00:01:20.022
Finally, at the top, see links won,
e-mails sent, your reply and win rates,

00:01:20.072 --> 00:01:21.508
and the days a link takes.

00:01:22.571 --> 00:01:27.121
Open Results by opportunity type
to see which openings win most.

00:01:27.171 --> 00:01:30.371
Subject lines being tested
compares two styles,

00:01:30.421 --> 00:01:32.348
until there are enough sends to tell.

00:01:33.321 --> 00:01:38.255
Every conversation and every reply sits
in one place, so no link slips away.

00:01:39.321 --> 00:01:43.046
Good to know: out-of-office
replies aren't counted as replies.

00:01:43.096 --> 00:01:45.023
The next e-mail simply waits.

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:50.738
So, follow your pitches, read and edit
a reply, send it in the same thread,

00:01:50.788 --> 00:01:53.380
mark the link won, and
see what works best.

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:58.582
Next, add listings and
redirects, in tutorial 9.7.
